cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MOF Functional-Group-Editing Database (MOF-Edit-DB)
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.TODO
authors:
  - name: "[Authors — to be completed]"
date-released: "2026-08-30"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  191,687 pore-measured metal-organic framework (MOF) records built by
  systematic linker functional-group editing, each assembled with pormake,
  relaxed with UFF4MOF/LAMMPS and measured with Zeo++ under one protocol.
  135,283 edited records carry the measured pore-limiting diameter of the
  same unedited parent scaffold, giving one-to-one before/after
  functionalization contrasts (Delta-PLD), plus a 77,161-asset QC-cleaned
  edited-edge bank with SMILES and SHA256-tracked 3D structures.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - pore limiting diameter
  - functional group editing
  - linker functionalization
  - high-throughput screening
  - machine-learning benchmark
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahian-lee/mof_edit_database"
